From c5a36c428594c2f62b8c5c5858416b89877fd118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/57] Z 6III: standby runs to the end -- the cores' WFI
 status, core hold, DDR self-refresh, the power-hold line

An untouched boot stopped at kernel ~68 s on
  Z63_UNMAPPED read addr=0x00c86a010 size=4 pc=0x0082010a0
That is the camera going to standby: 30 s after live view starts, the
application's auto-power-off timer (AppC_Tim at 0xa03389c50; the
duration from sub_40D65648, settings item 0x1521 = 5, 30 s) posts
0x3000003 (handled at 0x40d5a7a4), the EXPEED tells the MCU (family 1
kind 8 mode 08, then mode 06 and a 106-byte wake mask), saves the
settings journal, Linux enters s2idle, and the power-down the standby
path copies to WorkSRAM, sub_4019502C, runs on CPU0. Each of its steps
now has its device:

  - 0x0c86a010, the cores' WFI status (new, z63_cpustat_read): bit n is
    core n halted in WFI or switched off. The loop at 0x401950a0 waits
    for cores 1 and 2; the CPU3 off routine at 0x40179f50 holds core 3
    only when bit 3 is up. ../z9-qemu answers a constant 6.
  - 0x0d154344 core bits 1..3, the reset controller's set window: the
    power-down holds cores 1 and 2 (0x40195170) and 0x40179f80 holds
    core 3. It used to stop as "not modelled"; the core is now switched
    off as PSCI CPU_OFF does and its release bit drops, so a later
    release starts it afresh.
  - the DDR channels' self-refresh handshake (z63_ddr_broadcast): the
    0x138xxxxx instance writes to all four channels, and the channels'
    +0x7940 answers +0x7800 = 0x100 / 0x200 with 0x10 / 0, and +0x7458
    bit 0 acknowledges a bit-16 request, low on the first read after it.
    The same handshake is what the DDR frequency change sub_418422B8
    waits on (+0x7458 == 0x80010001). DECLARED: immediate.
  - GPIO_TOP port 3 bit 11 low, the power-hold line: driven high by the
    pin setup at boot (sub_41187B00, 0xffff0800), low only as the last
    store before WFI here (0x401952e8) and in the loader's and the
    emergency power-off (0x40093628, 0x40c08020). New machine property
    power-off: "shutdown" (default) requests a guest shutdown, as a
    camera that switched itself off -- -action shutdown=pause keeps the
    VM; "continue" only logs it.

Checked: an untouched boot now logs the cores' status 0xe, cores 1 and
2 held from WFI, and the power-hold drop at pc 0x82012e8, then shuts
down cleanly.

What the MCU does with the line, and waking from standby on a key, are
not modelled; the line is not in the default mcu-wires=. (The MCU's
power manager cuts the EXPEED's rails but DRAM's when its input reads
low after the power-off frame, and on a key restores them and raises a
resume flag the EXPEED reads on port 3 bit 6 -- a warm reboot with
DRAM kept, not a jump back.)

The live view's histogram (the second DISP press stopped on
0x15430104): the RSZ E unit, 0x15430100, is configured by sub_40C2767C
and started each frame (+0x00 = 1, 0x40c27670); z63-lv-frame-done now
admits those words (bits as each store sets them) and lets a start arm
E's next frame end, as its enable does, and the board maps the
resizer's histogram RAM at 0x15c00000 (0xc00, read by sub_40C2662C).
DECLARED: the bins read 0, an empty histogram. DISP now cycles through
the histogram screen.

Also from a sweep of every fixed device address the image materialises
against the board's windows, registers the firmware names that were
still unmapped:
  - SENSOR-IF: device 0x190's third and fourth banks, 0x15085000 and
    0x15085400 (+0x24, +0x108, +0x110, +0x118, +0x11c, the acknowledge
    words of sub_40C29C98/CCC/D34/D68), the window now 0x5800; device
    0x18e's +0x54 and +0x60 (sub_40C2B4C8, sub_40C2B5D4);
  - ISP-APB device 0x1a0: +0x2dc, +0x2e8, +0x2f4 (sub_40C1FBC8);
  - devices 0x1cc/0x1cd/0x1ce: the eight channels the loop at
    0x40c0b048 programs at +0x1000 i + 0x400 j (+0x144..+0x21c), the
    windows 0x2000;
  - device 0x184 at 0x15280000, a four-channel engine (new,
    nikon-z63-dev184.h);
  - EXS1784: 19 words and the +0x2700 table the driver reads outside the
    range its set was generated from.
All storage, each set and its evidence in its header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
